<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply raised in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply raised in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said it added liquidity to the money market in the week to May 15 in order to offset a seasonal rise in note circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  20.60 (-  3.23)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 116.09 (+  9.98)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   481.63 (+  7.84)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
